                        "review": "This is one of my favorite games. It combines two of my favorite things: Papers, Please and GTA lol \n\nThings were a little clunky starting off, but once I learned the systems and what the game expected, I had the time of my life. I finished campaign mode and started endless mode only to discover endless mode has 10x more upgrades and things to fix up than campaign mode. Which means I can easily get another 30 hours out of this game. \n\nWell done. \n\nThings I’d fix:\n\n-I need to be able to check off an item I’ve reviewed already. Currently you can only mark off items on the checklist that the person failed at, so I lose my place a lot when I pause the game. \n-The inventory system is too messy. It adds to the challenge, which is great, but if I have 5 of the same knife or piece of contraband, I should be able to consolidate them to one slot. \n-Tutorial could’ve been a little more thorough in some places. The handbook is really dense and hard to read so it’s not great for referencing. I’ve had to look a lot up. \n\nOther than that. Love this game. Would play again and again.",
